concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 December 1984 ([1989] ATS 21);"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "(f) the Convention on the Rights of the Child done at New York on 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4); (g) the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities done at New York on 13 December 2006 ([2008] ATS 12). Note: In 2011, the text of an international agreement in the Australian Treaty Series was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library on the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au). member means a member of the Committee. rule-maker has the same meaning as in the Legislation Act 2003. the Committee means the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Human Rights for the time being constituted under this Act.   Preliminary  Part 1  Section 3 Human Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011 Compilation date: 12/06/2024 Registered: 21/06/2024 (2) In the definition of human rights in subsection (1), the reference to the rights and freedoms recognised or declared by an international instrument is to be read as a reference to the rights and freedoms recognised or declared by the instrument as it applies to Australia." ;
    skos:definition "(f) the Convention on the Rights of the Child done at New York on 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4); (g) the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities done at New York on 13 December 2006 ([2008] ATS 12). Note: In 2011, the text of an international agreement in the Australian Treaty Series was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library on the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au). member means a member of the Committee. rule-maker has the same meaning as in the Legislation Act 2003. the Committee means the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Human Rights for the time being constituted under this Act.   Preliminary  Part 1  Section 3 Human Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011 Compilation date: 12/06/2024 Registered: 21/06/2024 (2) In the definition of human rights in subsection (1), the reference to the rights and freedoms recognised or declared by an international instrument is to be read as a reference to the rights and freedoms recognised or declared by the instrument as it applies to Australia."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9214a37150248b80d8c7cba1203b916f3c3a9d5070c444bce8b21706b865fe81" ;
    cof:pageNumber "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "List of international agreements accessible through the Australian Treaties Library." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
